{"id": "EUVD-2026-108841", "enisaUuid": "a9792d8f-1e49-3763-816d-7260c46e1161", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ngve: fix XSK buffer leak on error descriptor\n\nWhen the error bit is set in the RX completion descriptor, the buf_state\nand its attached buffer should be freed. In the case of AF_XDP ZC, the\nXSK buffer was not freed, leading to a leak.\n\nThis issue was caught by LLM.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:22:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:22:10", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/06656aaa7e43ae62b673c2244d27099b8b94a70d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/889f763874855c575429f75946132a53c573aa14", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9fed6a8ab8a5bacba2c709cb19d2dd6d2fa9112e"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99046"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "22e762bb-c8ed-3435-9512-0fdbc7ed9564", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.17"}, {"id": "2b53ec93-f307-319b-8629-74d30ee44701", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c1fffc5d66a7147d557736c2341a511e0896d9ff <9fed6a8ab8a5bacba2c709cb19d2dd6d2fa9112e"}, {"id": "420f187a-1a90-3b35-a475-7f8cae234c29", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c1fffc5d66a7147d557736c2341a511e0896d9ff <889f763874855c575429f75946132a53c573aa14"}, {"id": "5b1493da-e9a5-3ff1-9dc1-3fc8dd6e525d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "5ef97d26-8353-3602-8119-623c9d4772df", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c1fffc5d66a7147d557736c2341a511e0896d9ff <06656aaa7e43ae62b673c2244d27099b8b94a70d"}, {"id": "779733c5-d1d5-3298-95ce-573f0fb0a389", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "b9ea5d05-04e5-3b7d-b28f-faabc61b2d24", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendo